    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d462">

                <pb facs="0637" n="351" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg351"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2275</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-28T17:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 28, 1916, 5 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.20 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3872. Sir Edward Grey has again informed me that he expects the English and
                    French answer to our long note on shipping to be <pb facs="0638" n="352"
                        xml:id="pg352"/> ready next week. The English answer is now before the
                    Cabinet and he is urging the French to haste. He expresses regret at the long
                    time consumed and wishes me to assure you that he is hastening the answer as
                    urgently as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
